# Real DevSecOps Examples

---

## Environment Variables

```javascript
const port = process.env.PORT ?? 3000;
```

If `PORT` isn't defined

```
3000
```

is used.

---

## Reading Configuration

```javascript
const timeout =
config?.network?.timeout ?? 5000;
```

---

## API Responses

```javascript
const username =
response?.user?.name ?? "Unknown User";
```

---

## Deployment Script

```javascript
const region =
process.env.AWS_REGION ?? "ap-south-1";
```

---

# Common Mistakes

### Mistake 1

Using

```javascript
||
```

when

```javascript
??
```

is needed.

---

### Mistake 2

Using optional chaining everywhere.

Example

```javascript
user?.name
```

If you know `user` always exists

Simply write

```javascript
user.name
```

Optional chaining should be used when values may legitimately be missing.

---

### Mistake 3

Writing nested ternary operators.

Avoid code that's difficult to understand.

---

# Best Practices

✔ Prefer `===`

✔ Prefer `??` over `||` when dealing with configuration values

✔ Use Optional Chaining when reading API responses

✔ Avoid nested ternary operators

✔ Keep expressions readable

